    "result_text": "All tests pass. Here's a summary of the change.\n\n## What I implemented\n\nThe `POST /api/owners` request now accepts an optional ISO `birthDate`, and the owner response carries a derived `ageBand` of `MINOR` (< 18), `ADULT` (18\u201364) or `SENIOR` (65+), computed as completed years between `birthDate` and the owner's (resolved) `registrationDate`.\n\nI followed the existing patterns for owner-derived fields rather than adding a new pipeline step, since `ageBand` is a pure function of stored owner fields (like `locality`, `contactPreference`, `membershipLevel`):\n\n- **`model/AgeBand.java`** (new) \u2014 an enum with `forOwner(Owner)` holding the banding logic, mirroring `ContactPreference`/`MembershipLevel`. Returns `null` when either date is absent.\n- **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added the persisted `birthDate` field (`@Column(name = \"birth_date\")`) with getter/setter, alongside `registrationDate`.\n- **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added the `ageBand` mapping expression + a small `ageBand(owner)` helper that delegates to `AgeBand`. `birthDate` maps automatically by name.\n- **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 `birthDate` added to `OwnerFields` (request, `format: date`); `ageBand` added to `Owner` (response, `readOnly`). These regenerate `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto`.\n- **`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`** \u2014 added the `birth_date DATE` column so the JPA entity persists.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `AcceptanceTest.coreDerivesAgeBand` (birthDate `1990-01-01` \u2192 `ADULT`): passes.\n- Full suite: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\nNote the pipeline resolves `registrationDate` (default-to-today, rolled to a business day) before save, and the mapper runs at respond time, so `ageBand` is measured against the same stored `registrationDate` the spec calls for.",
